.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I tried the PR (didn't look at the code) and went over some of the trees the alternating row colors were applied to, and it is indeed very nice on those tables. It really does help with readability of wide tree items.\r\n\r\nI also agree that this should be disabled by default.\r\n\r\nAre these color guide colors exposed though style boxes when users add their own Tree nodes and style them? I couldn't find this out quickly in my test project.\r\n\r\nIMO we should be careful not to add it to too many trees; especially ones with only one column and that aren't very wide. I think trees like the SceneTree and FileSystem do not need the alternating row colors because they are not wide by default and don't really behave as tables. @passivestar will have an opinion on this that may be more specific than mine, but IMO from what I checked the ones you already applied this to seem fine.","state":"APPROVED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111283#pullrequestreview-3903604406","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/111283","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111283#pullrequestreview-3903604406"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/111283"}},"submitted_at":"2026-03-06T13:01:41Z","commit_id":null},{"id":4114171107,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc71OUTj","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?u=68d23e7ee9cdf810da125e8510b72f845b9dccc8&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Tested locally, it works as expected. Code looks good to me.\n\nThe feature is off by default, so that projects upgrading don't have their theming changed.\n\nNeeds a rebase.\n\n### Modern\n\nDark | Light\n-|-\n<img width=\"1350\" height=\"260\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9267c6ea-9b9c-451c-94d2-d4de67245bed\" /> | <img width=\"1350\" height=\"260\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/60123d2a-a474-4b31-8fd8-ac7e750c0800\" />\n\n### Classic\n\nDark | Light\n-|-\n<img width=\"1350\" height=\"296\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f0e123ab-4f25-47b4-973c-0a621ae0bb79\" /> | <img width=\"1350\" height=\"296\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b2ef96fc-5451-4c49-95d9-cfe9edbe1e79\" />","state":"APPROVED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/